# Deploy when needed (no “please deploy” handoffs)

When a change **only takes effect after deployment** (e.g. PlastyPesa **Lambda/API** in `plastypesa-backend-api`), the agent must **run deployment itself** after tests pass—**do not** end the task with “you need to deploy” unless deployment is **impossible** from this environment.

## What to do

1. After `npm test` and `npm run build:lambda` succeed, **deploy** using the repo’s normal path (typically AWS CDK from `plastypesa-backend-api`, e.g. `npx cdk deploy` / stack name the project uses). Prefer whatever is documented in that repo’s README or existing scripts.
2. If deploy **fails**, report the **command output** and what blocked it (credentials, MFA, wrong profile, approval prompts).
3. Only ask the owner to deploy when something **cannot** be automated here: **missing AWS/session**, **manual approval**, **secrets not available**, or **physical MFA**—and say **exactly** why the agent cannot run it.

## What not to do

- Do not treat “merge + push” as sufficient when the **running API** must change for the feature to work.
- Do not default to telling the owner to deploy as a **routine** closing step.

## Mobile / admin

- **Mobile**: store release / Play Console steps may still need the owner; backend behavior changes still require **API deploy** first.
- **Admin dashboard**: static hosting or separate pipeline—deploy the **same way** the project already uses when the change must go live.

This rule exists so shipping stays **agent-complete** whenever the toolchain allows it.
